I've got a Valkyrie on an amulet ascension run. I've paused at level
four because I've ascended a Valk before, maybe even genocideless (as
this is), and I'm toying with the amusement value of dying and leaving
all my juicy gear in a bones file (on the antisymmetric.com server).

The list of artifacts I've managed acquire is pretty interesting in
itself... I made a relatively early wish for Grayswandir, and of
course I got  Mjollnir as a sacrifice gift and Vorpal at crowning, but
I also found Sunsword and the Heart of Ahriman... and plus there's the
useless artifacts (Dragonbane, Trollsbane, Ogresmasher) I could take
some puckish delight the certainty I'd be crippling the finder's
chance of wishing for other artifacts, on top of the christmas
presents I'd be leaving behind. And of course, because I'm not a
spellcaster, I have a nice library of everything from light, knock,
and lock, to finger of death and create familiar.

First, I'm wondering what people think about this idea.

Second, if I were going to do it, what would be the optimal level? I'm
not just talking about optimizing probability that I'll leave a bones
file; obviously the level above the bottom of Gehennom would be the
best likelihood. I'm talking about balance between leaving Christmas
presents and leaving them to a character that is likely to get good
use of them... Maybe the mines, a level or two down from the store? Or
one level south of Sokoban? Hmmm.

